.\" Manual page for duckling.
.\"
.\" It exists because the binary takes arguments and has no --help to
.\" describe them: src/main.rs queues every argument and nothing else, so
.\" this is the only place that is written down, and lintian tags a binary
.\" without a page.
.\"
.\" @VERSION@ is substituted by packaging/debian/build-deb.sh, the same way
.\" control.in is, so the version in the header cannot drift from the package.
.\" The date is the date this page was last revised and not the build date,
.\" which is the convention and is also what makes the page reproducible.
.\"
.\" Author: David M. Anderson
.\" Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
.TH DUCKLING 1 "2026\-09\-04" "duckling @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
duckling \- convert documents to Markdown, JSON, DocLang or LaTeX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duckling
.RI [ file | folder \ ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Duckling
converts documents on the machine it runs on. Word, PowerPoint, Excel, PDF,
HTML, EPUB, RTF, OpenDocument, Apple iWork, email, Visio and some forty other
formats go in; DocLang, Markdown, docling JSON, a DocLang archive or LaTeX
comes out.
Files are queued from the command line, from a drop on the window or from
the Add buttons; a folder contributes every file under it that can be read.
Nothing converts until Convert is pressed, so the format and destination
chosen at that moment apply to the whole batch.
.PP
Output goes beside each source file or into one folder. An existing file is
never overwritten: a second
.I report.md
becomes
.IR "report (1).md" .
.PP
Scanned PDFs and images are read by layout, table\-structure and OCR models
installed under
.IR /usr/lib/duckling ,
so nothing is downloaded after installation and nothing is sent anywhere.
The converter is docling.rs, the Rust port of IBM's Docling.
.SH OPTIONS
There are none.
.B duckling
is a window rather than a command\-line interface. For a command\-line
converter over the same engine, see docling.rs's own
.BR docling\-rs .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I file
A document to queue. A file whose extension docling.rs does not read is
reported in the window's status line.
.TP
.I folder
A folder to queue: every readable file under it, in name order, files before
subfolders. Files that cannot be read are skipped without comment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns success when the window has been closed. A non\-zero status means the
window could not be created at all \(em no display, or no usable graphics
driver \(em rather than anything about a document.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/duckling/models
The ONNX models for the PDF and image pipeline.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/duckling/pdfium
The pdfium library, loaded by name at run time.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/duckling.desktop
The desktop entry, which lists the document types Duckling reads so that a
file manager offers it under Open With.
.SH SEE ALSO
The converter is documented at https://github.com/docling\-project/docling.rs,
and the design of this application in DESIGN.md in its own repository at
https://github.com/excelano/duckling.
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson
